# Testing new Debug Monitor in old Debug Monitor
```
AlphaPC164LX> flload lx164sft.img 900000
AlphaPC164LX> go
```

# Starting Debug Monitor on AlphaPC 164LX
1. Copy lx164dbm.rom (in ebboot/lx164/) to floppy
2. Enable fail-safe booter: Set CF7 on J27 (System Configuration Jumpers)
3. Power on
4. After 1-2-3 beeps loading starts

You can use standard ISA POST Code diagnostic card to see boot codes.

# AlphaPC 164LX SROM
I replaced SROM chip with reprogrammable [AT17LV256](https://www.microchip.com/en-us/product/at17lv256). It doesn't matter if the chip has more capacity than original.  
After building ```ebfw/srom``` the produced ihex file ```ebboot/lx164/lx164_sr.hex``` can be programmed with [Atmel CPS](https://www.microchip.com/en-us/development-tool/configurator-programming-system).

# AT17LV256 programming with [Atmel CPS](https://www.microchip.com/en-us/development-tool/configurator-programming-system)
In Windows 2000 the installer fails to install ```tvichw32.dll```.  
Running the installer .exe with ```/a``` flag allows to give temproary directory where files are extracted.  
Copy ```tvichw32.dll``` to ```\winnt\system32```.  

Following programming settings work:
* Procedure: /E
* Family: AT6K/Other
* Device: AT17LV256(A) (256K)
* Reset Polarity: High

If you don't have the official [ATDH2200E CONFIGURATOR PROGRAMMING KIT](https://www.microchip.com/en-us/development-tool/atdh2200e) it is easy to build one on a breadboard using [the schematics](https://ww1.microchip.com/downloads/en/DeviceDoc/doc0642.pdf).  
I used a 5V power supply.

# 21174 PYXIS in AlphaPC 164LX
Enabling ```MC_MCR_M_PIPELINE_CACHE``` causes ```LED_F_MEMCHECKSUM``` error.  
Disabling ```MC_MCR_M_OVERLAP_DISABLE``` (overlap enabled) causes memory errors.  
